    "task_type": "study_forensics",
    "prompt": "Two independent studies compared learning support systems based on language models with human tutors. In the first study, students using an AI assistant achieved a success rate of 66 percent compared to 61 percent with human tutoring and 56 percent with written hints. Tutors confirmed 76.4 percent of AI answers without major corrections. A second study with an AI tool to support tutoring sessions increased topic mastery by 4 percentage points; for inexperienced tutors, the advantage was as high as 9 points. The authors emphasize that AI does not replace human tutoring but complements it.\n",
    "context": "Two small but randomized studies with concrete success rates. The text avoids\noverstatement and positions AI as complementary, not replacing human tutors.\nModerate effect sizes honestly reported.\n",
    "expected_answer": "solid",
    "reference_solution": "Two randomized studies report moderate performance improvements with AI-based tutoring support. The text avoids overclaims, reports concrete metrics, and positions AI as complementary to human instruction. Despite small sample sizes, the claims match the evidence.\n",
